---
/**
 * Two overlapping intervals that mean opposite things, and the animation that tells them apart.
 *
 * Both rows are measured: the same sweep, 160 games per condition, the intervals `rukh eval sweep`
 * printed. The top row is the pair the acceptance criterion names first (`<w1500>` and `<w2000>`),
 * whose point estimates are eleven Elo apart; the bottom row is the outer pair of the same three
 * conditions (`<w1500>` and `<w2400>`), ninety-five apart.
 *
 * The animation shrinks every interval the way more games would, all four at the same rate,
 * because that is the only thing more games buy. The bottom pair comes apart; the top pair never
 * does, since the two centres barely move and an interval cannot shrink past its own centre. That
 * is the whole difference between "not enough games" and "no difference", and it is the reason the
 * milestone stopped paying for `<w2000>` and kept paying for the other two.
 *
 * The numbers next to each row are the ones `labs/m4/games_needed.py` prints from those scores;
 * the motion repeats what they say rather than adding anything, which is why parking it under
 * `prefers-reduced-motion` loses nothing.
 */
const LOW = 1460;
const HIGH = 1730;
const x = (elo: number) => 150 + ((elo - LOW) / (HIGH - LOW)) * 465;

interface Band {
  label: string;
  elo: number;
  lo: number;
  hi: number;
}

const rows: { y: number; bands: [Band, Band]; verdict: string; games: string }[] = [
  {
    y: 64,
    bands: [
      { label: '<w1500>', elo: 1549, lo: 1481, hi: 1609 },
      { label: '<w2000>', elo: 1538, lo: 1479, hi: 1597 },
    ],
    verdict: 'no hay diferencia',
    games: '24 420 partidas',
  },
  {
    y: 150,
    bands: [
      { label: '<w1500>', elo: 1549, lo: 1481, hi: 1609 },
      { label: '<w2400>', elo: 1644, lo: 1578, hi: 1707 },
    ],
    verdict: 'faltan partidas',
    games: '357 partidas',
  },
];

const ticks = [1500, 1550, 1600, 1650, 1700];
---

<figure class="fig fig--shrink">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 640 230"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Dos pares de condiciones con sus intervalos del 95 por ciento. Arriba, w1500 en 1549 y w2000 en 1538: los centros están a once puntos de Elo y los intervalos no se separan por muchas partidas que se jueguen, harían falta 24 420 por condición. Abajo, w1500 en 1549 y w2400 en 1644: noventa y cinco puntos de distancia, y con 357 partidas por condición los intervalos se separan."
  >
    <g font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--muted)">
      {rows.map((row) => (
        <g>
          <text x="10" y={row.y - 14} fill="var(--ink)" font-size="10">
            {row.verdict}
          </text>
          {row.bands.map((band, index) => (
            <g>
              <text x="10" y={row.y + index * 26 + 4} font-size="10">
                {band.label}
              </text>
              <g
                class={`fig-shrink__band fig-shrink__band--${index}`}
                style={`--centre:${x(band.elo)}px`}
              >
                <rect
                  x={x(band.lo)}
                  y={row.y + index * 26 - 7}
                  width={x(band.hi) - x(band.lo)}
                  height="11"
                  rx="2"
                  fill={index === 0 ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--diagram-stroke)'}
                  fill-opacity="0.22"
                  stroke={index === 0 ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--line)'}
                  stroke-width="0.8"
                />
                <line
                  x1={x(band.elo)}
                  y1={row.y + index * 26 - 9}
                  x2={x(band.elo)}
                  y2={row.y + index * 26 + 6}
                  stroke={index === 0 ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--ink)'}
                  stroke-width="1.4"
                />
              </g>
              <text x={x(band.elo)} y={row.y + index * 26 + 16} text-anchor="middle" font-size="9">
                {band.elo}
              </text>
            </g>
          ))}
          <text x="10" y={row.y + 44} font-size="9" fill="var(--accent-text-aa)">
            {row.games}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))}

      <line x1="150" y1="204" x2="615" y2="204" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="0.8"></line>
      {ticks.map((elo) => (
        <text x={x(elo)} y="218" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9">
          {elo}
        </text>
      ))}
      <text x="10" y="218" font-size="9">
        Elo medido
      </text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="caption">
    Los cuatro intervalos se estrechan al mismo ritmo, que es lo único que compran más partidas. El
    par de abajo se separa; el de arriba no se separa nunca, porque sus centros están a once puntos.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
